    "Scouting Notes": "Definitely can't catch, and Brewers seem to have accepted that. 1B/DH only.\n Not awful at first base, but lacks range (Rowdy Tellez type defender). Not very tall for a 1B.\n Best chance at MLB success is as a Dan Vogelbach type, but he doesn't have the hit tool Vogelbach has.\n Takes a ton of walks, has big power that he can't always get to in game.\n Like him a lot more from the left hand side, but the stats aren't bad from the right side.\n Doubt he's a major leaguer but if the hit tool improves a bit, he could be a weak side platoon guy for a team with a bad DH.",
